T. I added LFRF as an alias to Logseq/Flashcard/Review/Favorite so that on iPhone I can search for that acronym instead.",[]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-374","import into garden For iOS iPadOS users (Working Copy) · charliie-dev/Logseq-Git-Sync-101 Wiki",["Managed to setup my Logseq/Flashcards on my iPhone for the first time. A bit tricky to set up, then works okay. almost too slow to be useful in this garden on i"]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-578","Microsoft's Person/Satya Nadella is building himself a personal context portfolio that includes discussions from others at MS",[]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-710","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zqEZyHkXgh0&t=1460s",["Microsoft's Person/Satya Nadella is building himself a personal context portfolio that includes discussions from others at MS"]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-1447","Filed",[]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-1461","My/Principle/Explicit is better than Implicit",["Filed"]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-1514","GitHub/Codespace/Q/What does the Install App dialog do when opening a GitHub Codespace?",["Filed"]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-1609","Foam",["Filed"]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-1621","Foam/GitHub",["Filed"]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-1640","Person/Jani Eväkallio",["Filed"]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-1670","Foam/Q/How can I configure Foam to use a subfolder as the workspace root?",["Filed"]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-1751","Foam/Q/How can I rename a Foam page so that all wikilinks to it are renamed too?",["Filed"]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-1839","Foam/Q/Does Foam have an alias feature like Obsidian does?",["Filed"]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-1905","VSCode/Q/Is there a keyboard shortcut mappable item in settings for maximize panel for the terminal?",["Filed"]],["2026-06-15%20Mon/","source-block-2013","GitHub/Codespace/Q/Does starting tmux in a GitHub Codespace keep it alive?",["Filed"]],["2026-06-16%20Tue/","block-6a316c16-3f53-4015-8466-97688bcb8aac","Lessons Learned from Mollick's Choosing to Stay Human",[]],["2026-06-16%20Tue/","source-block-100","I recently read Ethan Mollick's Choosing to Stay Human (One Useful Thing) and I was reminded about a distinction between",["Lessons Learned from Mollick's Choosing to Stay Human"]],["2026-06-16%20Tue/","source-block-288","Cognitive offloading - using tools to extend what you can do (notes, calculators, search). Historically benign, often beneficial.",["Lessons Learned from Mollick's Choosing to Stay Human"]],["2026-06-16%20Tue/","source-block-427","Cognitive surrender - when the tool does your thinking and you stop trying. Mollick mentions a BCG consultant study where professional consultants abandoned critical thinking when AI gave confident-sounding wrong answers. This implies that the \"default\" interaction with AI seems to be one of cognitive surrender rather than cognitive offloading",["Lessons Learned from Mollick's Choosing to Stay Human"]],["2026-06-16%20Tue/","source-block-846","He talks about two separate papers from the same Wharton team (Bastani et al.) reach apparently opposite conclusions w.r.t AI's ability to help learning:",["Lessons Learned from Mollick's Choosing to Stay Human"]],["2026-06-16%20Tue/","source-block-1003","AI is detrimental to learning - Turkish high school math - ChatGPT for homework → better homework scores, worse unassisted test performance. Shortcutting the struggle shortcutted the learning.",["Lessons Learned from Mollick's Choosing to Stay Human"]],["2026-06-16%20Tue/","source-block-1271","AI can help learning if it produces optimal friction - Taipei Python course - have AI sequence practice problems matched to student knowledge state) → +0.15 standard deviation on final exams, ≈ 6–9 months of schooling. Same researchers, different outcome.",["Lessons Learned from Mollick's Choosing to Stay Human"]]],"format_version":5}